    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 1st with a condensed lineup, as the team looks to maximize efficiency while managing our strict 5x5 Roto game caps. **Christian Yelich** is our undeniable anchor today; projected at a score of 63.76, he benefits from a premier leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon advantage against Roupp. While **Carson Benge** also cracks the 50-point threshold, the middle of our infield faces a tougher gauntlet. **Junior Caminero** remains a start despite an intimidating matchup against Madden (2.31 xERA), as his high base projection and spot in the cleanup role provide enough leverage to weather the poor SP matchup. Conversely, we are keeping **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, and **Colt Keith** in the lineup as foundational pieces, though their output is capped by moderate xERA profiles from their respective opposing starters.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just shy of our 40.0 efficiency floor with a 36.86 score. The optimizer ultimately sidelined **Chase Meidroth** due to the high-skill profile of the opposing pitcher, Ryan, which neutralized the potential gains from a hitter-friendly park. Similarly, **Dillon Dingler** (36.54) and **Casey Schmitt** (36.40) were relegated to the bench; while **Dillon Dingler** benefits from a strong xwOBA, his negative platoon split against Jax made him an inefficient play compared to our active starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Yordan Alvarez**, who remains sidelined during this off-day to preserve his game cap, alongside depth options like **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom are currently held in reserve.\n\nRisks for today include the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**. Should official lineups indicate a drop in the batting order for either, their efficiency scores will likely dip below the optimal threshold. We are also wary of the base stealing environment; while **Colt Keith** benefits from a slow delivery matchup, we are missing our primary speed threats today. We will continue to evaluate weather patterns and late-breaking injury news to ensure our 40-point floor remains an effective barrier against cap depletion.",
